  "payload": {
    "rawResponseText": "For an owner in Europe who wants to **preserve individuality** while joining a larger distribution and loyalty platform, the most relevant options are the major **soft brands / collection brands** from Marriott, Hilton, Hyatt, Accor, IHG, Choice, Wyndham, and Best Western.[1][8][10][11][20]\n\nThe strongest brands to consider are:\n\n| Group | Soft brand / collection | Fit for an independent hotel |\n|---|---|---|\n| Marriott | **Autograph Collection**, **Tribute Portfolio**, **The Luxury Collection** | Allows distinctive hotels to keep their identity while gaining Marriott’s loyalty and commercial engine.[11][16][20] |\n| Hilton | **Curio Collection by Hilton**, **Tapestry Collection by Hilton**, **LXR Hotels & Resorts** | Designed for independent or boutique properties that want flexibility plus Hilton distribution and loyalty access.[8][10][16] |\n| Hyatt | **The Unbound Collection by Hyatt**, **Destination by Hyatt**, **JdV by Hyatt** | Focused on individuality, local character, and a softer brand overlay than a standard hard brand.[10][12] |\n| Accor | **MGallery Collection**, **Handwritten Collection** | Explicitly positioned around personality-led, distinctive hotels; Accor has been expanding this model in Europe and globally.[3][7] |\n| IHG | **Vignette Collection** | A newer collection concept for independent hotels that want to retain their own identity while joining a global system.[10][11] |\n| Choice | **Ascend Hotel Collection** | A soft-brand option for independent hotels seeking affiliation without losing uniqueness.[11][15][16] |\n| Wyndham | **Trademark Collection by Wyndham**, **Registry Collection Hotels** | Targets independent hotels that want affiliation, with Trademark especially positioned for boutique and upscale properties.[10][12] |\n| Best Western | **BW Premier Collection**, **BW Signature Collection**, **Sure Hotel Collection** | Offers multiple soft-brand tiers, including options for upper-upscale and more midscale independent hotels.[5] |\n\nFor **Europe specifically**, the most commonly cited and credible choices in the results are **Marriott Autograph Collection**, **Hilton Curio/Tapestry**, **Hyatt Unbound/Destination/JdV**, **Accor MGallery/Handwritten**, and **Best Western’s BW collections**, because these are explicitly described as keeping a hotel’s personality while linking it to a major distribution network.[3][5][8][10][11][13][20]\n\nIf you want, I can narrow this to the **best soft brands by segment** in Europe, for example **luxury**, **upper-upscale**, or **midscale**.",
